        How Accurate Are These Tests?
      </h2>
      <p
        style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text2);line-height:1.7;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem;"
      >
        Every browser-based test has real limits — event coalescing, OS
        scheduling, and background CPU load can all affect a reading. We'd
        rather explain that than hide it behind a single impressive-looking
        number.
      </p>
      <div class="why-grid">
        <div class="why-card">
          <div class="why-card-title">⌨️ Keyboard</div>
          <div class="why-card-desc">
            Physical key → OS → browser event → measured press duration.
            Reliable for comparing keys against each other; not a substitute for
            a hardware scan-rate spec.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <div class="why-card-title">🖱 Mouse</div>
          <div class="why-card-desc">
            Mouse → OS → browser pointer events (using getCoalescedEvents where
            supported) → statistical analysis. Reliable up to roughly
            1500–2000Hz in most Chromium browsers; higher rates can be
            under-reported.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <div class="why-card-title">🖥️ Monitor</div>
          <div class="why-card-desc">
            Display → requestAnimationFrame → frame-timing analysis. Accurate to
            roughly ±1–2Hz under normal conditions, with a stability grade to
            flag when a reading isn't holding steady.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <div class="why-card-title">🟦 Screen</div>
          <div class="why-card-desc">
            Full-screen reference colors and patterns — the same principle used
            by dedicated dead pixel checkers. A browser can't read back what's
            physically displayed, so spotting a dead pixel or backlight bleed
            still needs your own eyes; this tool gives you the cleanest possible
            reference to check against.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="why-card">
          <div class="why-card-title">🎙️ Webcam/Mic/Speaker</div>
          <div class="why-card-desc">
            Camera → MediaStream track settings + live frame timing for FPS. Mic
            → Web Audio API for relative level, noise floor, and clipping — not
            a calibrated decibel reading. Speakers → real hard-panned tones per
            channel, so what you hear is exactly what's being sent.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
